{"name":"Stone Cold","hex":"#555555","fetched":"2026-10-16","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"stone cold","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Very cold ; lacking any semblance of warmth.","Lacking emotion or compassion."]},{"part":"Adverb","definitions":["Certainly; definitely; obviously."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/stone_cold"}],"entries":[{"title":"Stone Cold (Swindells novel)","blocks":[{"text":"Stone Cold is a young-adult novel by Robert Swindells, published by Heinemann in 1993. Set in Bradford and on the streets of London, the first-person narrative switches between Link, a newly-homeless young man adjusting to his situation, and Shelter, an ex-army officer scorned after being dismissed from his job, supposedly on \"medical grounds\", with a sinister motive."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/d/d1/Stone_Cold_cover.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Stone_Cold_(Swindells_novel)"},{"title":"Stone Cold (Parker novel)","blocks":[{"text":"Stone Cold is a crime novel by Robert B. Parker, the fourth in his Jesse Stone series."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/6/65/Stone_Cold_%28Robert_Parker_novel_-_cover_art%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Stone_Cold_(Parker_novel)"},{"title":"Stone Cold (1991 film)","blocks":[{"text":"Stone Cold is a 1991 action film directed by Craig R. Baxley and starring Brian Bosworth, Lance Henriksen and William Forsythe. The film's story centers on a biker gang in Mississippi that tries to assassinate district attorney Brent Whipperton and free Trouble Owens, one of their members who is about to be resentenced to death for the murder of a priest."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/8/82/Stone-Cold-poster.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unsca